Project (C++ / armadillo):
* calculate (2D) and plot (2D and 3D) the local density of a nuclear system
* calculate (2D) some associated geometrical properties
* optimize the local density calculation (2D)

=> use git, doxygen, make, cxxtest, remark.js, quadratures, mandatory unit tests
=> one mid-project presentation
=> for the second part of the project, use gitlab PRs only (only one project member with rw) !

1. prepare the project tree
2. implement the basis truncation (mandatory tests)
3. implement the basis functions calculation (mandatory tests)
4. implement the basis overlap calculation (mandatory tests)
5. implement the local density calculation (mandatory tests)
6. calculate and plot the local density
7. optimize the local density calculation
8. implement the observables calculation
9. BONUS: implement the exact observables calculation (using HO representation of the operators)

